  "area": "ARM core edges: ARM9/ARM7 instruction edges and the ARM9 CP15 (protection unit, TCM, caches)",
  "about": "Expected result-block values for the Quayholt rehearsal ROM, its per-pier demo ROMs and the release ROM's auto QA run, judged by tools/judge.py. Block layout: arm9/source/game/ledger.h. Every item reads one result code (values[1..30]: 1 = the behaviour GBATEK describes, 2/3 = known alternatives, 0xFF other, 0xFFFF never measured) or a prerequisite bit (values[31]) and carries \"done\": the completion bit of its pier in values[0]. \"frame\" is the minimum number of frames to run, per boot. \"known\" lists, per emulator version and renderer, the gating items expected to fail there; judge.py --profile passes only when the failing set matches exactly. Run melonDS with its JIT off (the interpreter is what the profiles record; headless mds.sh uses the interpreter). Items whose source is unconfirmed have no hardware evidence yet and are informational until the DS Lite run (docs/HW-QA.md).",
